# Everything under Prefabs/, Textures/, Data/ and the root .asset files is written by
# Editor/genassets.py, and that script emits LF. `genassets.py --check` compares bytes, so with
# core.autocrlf turning LF into CRLF on checkout every generated file looked stale forever: 25 of
# them, permanently, on a clean tree. A check that is always red is a check nobody reads.
#
# Pinning these to LF makes the comparison mean what it says. Nothing changes in git itself - the
# object database already holds LF - only what lands on disk.
*.asset   text eol=lf
*.prefab  text eol=lf
*.meta    text eol=lf
*.asmdef  text eol=lf

# Art is generated too, and a byte comparison on a PNG must never see a newline touched.
*.png     binary
